Star catalog provenance
=======================

bright.bin
  Magnitude-sorted naked-eye catalog carried by rn-site. Each record contains
  a J2000/ICRS direction, apparent magnitude, and display color.

Named-star callouts
  The 50-entry editorial pool in public/js/starscape-ui.js is position-matched
  to bright.bin. Names, spectral classifications, and parallaxes were checked
  against SIMBAD and the Hipparcos New Reduction (CDS VizieR I/311). Distances
  are rounded for legibility; values for luminous supergiants whose parallax is
  poorly constrained are approximate rather than false-precision reciprocals.

Gaia LOD
  public/stars/lod is generated from ESA Gaia DR3 gaia_source fields source_id,
  ra, dec, phot_g_mean_mag, and bp_rp with phot_g_mean_mag <= 12. It is produced
  offline by tools/build_star_lod.py. The web application never contacts ESA or
  CDS at runtime.

Sources
  ESA Gaia Archive: https://gea.esac.esa.int/archive/
  Gaia DR3 documentation: https://gea.esac.esa.int/archive/documentation/GDR3/
  SIMBAD: https://simbad.cds.unistra.fr/simbad/
  Hipparcos New Reduction: https://cdsarc.cds.unistra.fr/viz-bin/cat/I/311
